# An elf takes School Focus, and Necromancy is not on offer. (bd inc-q1ei)
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/school-focus-elf.keys 42
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS ALONGSIDE tools/keys/school-focus.keys. The guard that hides
# an already-focused school (src/Create.cpp) shares its Necromancy line with a
# second rule -- an elf may not focus on Necromancy at all:
#
#     if (!((focused & SC_NEC) || isMType(MA_ELF)))
#
# The duplicate-school half of that line was rewritten for inc-q1ei; the elf
# half was not, and this run is what says so. The orc in school-focus.keys
# cannot show it, because the ban never fires for him: his menu carries
# Necromancy on purpose.
#
# The character need do nothing after the menu is read, but the run must still
# reach a map: tools/headless.sh calls a session that never entered one NO
# GAMEPLAY and refuses to report it as a pass. So generation is carried to the
# end and the script stops on the first screen of the dungeon.
#
# Every choice here is a menu letter, and menu letters move when the list
# changes. Run with the seed and the settings named above.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes
e       # Race:     [e] Elf
a       # Subrace:  [a] Elf (Standard)
d       # Class:    [d] Mage
a       # Attributes: the first of the five offered sets
e       # Alignment: [e] Neutral

# The specialty list is chosen by name, not by letter: it is the same nine
# schools as the focus menu and it is ALREADY short of Necromancy for an elf,
# so every letter after Enchantment sits one place earlier than it does for
# the orc.
@expect "schools of magic"
@choose "Evocation"

# The feat list runs to 81 entries over two pages, and School Focus is on the
# second, so TAB comes before the name.
@expect "Choose a feat"
TAB
@choose "School Focus"
@expect "Choose a focus school:"
@dump:elf-school-menu
@choose "Abjuration"

# The rest of generation, none of which this run reads.
@expect "Choose a feat"
TAB
@choose "Spell Penetration"
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y # Done, and confirm keeping the ranks
@while "wish to worship" y
@expect "personality archetype"
a       # Personality archetype
@while "Learn which spell" a
@until "Things in View" ESC

# One turn of real play. tools/headless.sh writes logs/session.log on the first
# COMPLETED turn and reports a session without one as NO GAMEPLAY, so a script
# that stops the moment the map appears is refused rather than read.
.
@dump:elf-arrived
